{"diagnosis": "The last results (repair/tree_region and retrieval/deduction/layered_shallow & kernel_h4) show two clear patterns: (a) parsimony wins - visits:2 was promoted (retrieval 1.0, deduction 1.0) and is the single most reliable improvement in this arm; (b) aggressive recurrence/feedback changes backfire - cycles:2+rlt collapsed to 0.5176 and latent_steps:3+verifier_visits:2+visits:4 collapsed to 0.498, while ldt_projection was neutral-to-slightly-negative (0.9688 vs 0.978 predicted). For the research incumbent specifically, exact_by_visit is 0.7441 -> 0.7578 -> 0.7559: accuracy saturates after visit 2 and slightly declines at visit 3, so the recurrence is not the bottleneck - capacity for the prior-weighted variance term and feedback quality are. Expected information gain score = 8*Var_q(p_outcome1) - cost_weight*cost requires clean prior-weighted aggregation over 6 hypotheses plus a cost-vs-gain tradeoff; this is a shallow, near-set-function, so a 3-visit deep recurrence with 1 verifier call is over-parameterized and under-fed. Do NOT retry rlt feedback or cycles>=2 (both failed); do NOT add verifier_visits blindly (costs a call each).",
  "proposals": [
    {"config": {"visits": 2}, "rationale": "Exact-by-visit plateaus at visit 2 (0.7578) and declines at visit 3 (0.7559); removing the third visit cuts FLOPs ~1/3 (3346176 -> ~2.2e6) and one recurrence step, matching the visits:2 promotion pattern in retrieval and deduction. The objective 8*Var - cw*cost is a single scalar per candidate, reachable by one answer pass after the latent step, so the extra cycle mostly adds noise and overfitting to the deep-supervision loss.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.79, "falsification": "If measured dev_exact is below 0.7559 + 0.005 (i.e., < 0.761), this refutation holds - the plateau was noise and visit 3 was load-bearing."},
    {"config": {"hidden": 64}, "rationale": "The core computation is prior-weighted variance over 6 hypothesis likelihoods: Var = sum_i q_i p_i^2 - (sum_i q_i p_i)^2. With uniform prior (q_i=1/6) this is (1/6)*sum p_i^2 - (mean p)^2, a second-order statistic of the 6 likelihood features; hidden=32 may under-represent this quadratic interaction. Doubling hidden to 64 raises params modestly (~11.7k -> ~20k, still far below 250k) and gives the answer step room to represent the variance-minus-cost tradeoff without adding recurrence depth.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.80, "falsification": "If measured dev_exact is not higher than the incumbent by >0.005 (i.e., <= 0.761), the variance term is already representable at hidden=32 and extra capacity is wasted."},
    {"config": {"verifier_visits": 2}, "rationale": "The incumbent uses 1 verifier call per visit with direct feedback; the score 8*Var - cw*cost is sensitive to cost_weight (col 13) which is a per-instance scalar that is hard to infer from features alone. A second in-loop verifier diagnostic (verified/ok/diag0/diag1) per visit lets the answer step correct the cost-vs-gain tradeoff via the feedback channel. Cost is one extra verifier call per instance (verifier_calls 2.0 -> ~3.0), acceptable given accuracy-first promotion.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.79, "falsification": "If measured dev_exact is <= 0.761 or verifier_calls force a FLOPs/call regression that outweighs the gain, the feedback channel is not informative for this skill and the incumbent's 1-call setting is optimal."}
  ]
}
